"""PlayOnline OWN login responders -- replace the MITM relay with real answers.

One script, modes chosen by argv[1]:
    patch      TCP 54000  -- POLP version check; replays the canned cmd-8 reply
    directory  TCP 51240  -- IRC directory; mints a 300 greeting that redirects
                            the client to our auth node, then closes
    authcap    TCP 5124x  -- auth-node capture harness: mints its own 300 tokens,
                            logs the client's cleartext USER + encrypted NICK, and
                            (once we have the session key) will answer the login

Unlike stub.py (which relays to the real SE service), this file SERVES the client
itself. It shares config/server.yaml. The auth node still needs the session-cipher
key (K = RSA-KDF of the account token, constant per
account) before it can answer -- authcap exists to drive the
live login that lets us derive it.
"""
